  "$comment": "ALL 2.0 policy table: the ONE place where a number, a window or a limit of the end-to-end path is written down (plan section 0 and 7.1). The tunnel node (Go), the control plane (TypeScript) and the device (Python) read it; nobody copies a value into code (the contract generator lint fails the suite when one does). Units are in the key suffix: _s seconds, _bytes, _days, _pct percent. Keys listed in `provisional` are the plan's initial values: they are retuned after G0 and G1 and ONLY here. This is the node projection (the `copies` of the contract lint table): only the sections that runtime reads.",
